analysisWe need to create an assert statement corresponding to the comment.

Comment: 
```
// @@@ If the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the initial size of the list), then for every valid index less than the specified index, the element at that position remains unchanged or continues to be null if it was initially null.
```

We are in remove method. Preconditions: index valid: index >=0 && index < \old(this.size()) (initial size). Also they check checkInterval(index,0,size()-1) which ensures that.

We need to assert that for all i where 0 <= i < index, the element after removal at position i equals the element before removal at same position. Or if it was null before, remains null (that's same as equality). So spec: \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) ? but need handle null. Use (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)))? In JML, we can use == for reference equality, but for objects we may want .equals. However earlier examples used .equals for objects. Use (this.get(i) == null ? \old(this.get(i)) == null : this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))))? Simpler: this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) works if not null but will NPE if null. So better to use Objects.equals(this.get(i), \old(this.get(i))). But we need to use only publicly accessible observer methods; Objects.equals is static method from java.util.Objects, not part of this class. Might be allowed? In previous examples they used .equals directly; they assume non-null? The comment says "remains unchanged or continues to be null if it was initially null." So we need to allow both null and unchanged.

We can express as: (this.get(i) == null ? \old(this.get(i)) == null : this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))).

Thus overall assert: index>=0 && index<\old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<index; (this.get(i)==null ? \old(this.get(i))==null : this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))).

But need to reference size before removal: \old(this.size()).

Also need to ensure index is valid. So assert: (index>=0 && index<\old(this.size())) => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<index; (this.get(i)==null ? \old(this.get(i))==null : this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))));

Make sure parentheses correct.

Thus final answer.

